{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLNh4UZCeUAq4LexuSae","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`bug.apart(t)` now returns `-a*t + a/2 - a/(2*(2*t - 1))` instead of `-a*t`.\n\nThe cause was in `apart` in `sympy/polys/partfrac.py`. After `P.cancel(Q)`, the numerator was a polynomial over `ZZ[a]`, which is a ring, not a field. `P.div(Q, auto=True)` then did a truncating ring division and dropped the remainder (`-a/2`). I changed that line to `P.to_field().div(Q.to_field())`, so the division is exact.\n\nI ran `sympy/polys/tests/test_partfrac.py`: 10 tests pass and 1 fails. The one failure is `test_noncommutative_pseudomultivariate`. It fails the same way without my change, so it isn't caused by this fix. I didn't add a regression test, since the rules say not to edit test files.\n\nI left the identical `P.div(Q, auto=True)` call at line 336 (in `apart_list`) alone to keep the change minimal. It may have the same problem for symbolic coefficients, but I didn't check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":770,"cache_read_input_tokens":25864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":770},"output_tokens":368,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"556a750e-be73-42f5-8c3b-ff675071f5cd","uuid":"3f6ff44a-9291-45ef-9611-56bb0d3091b6","timestamp":"2026-11-23T19:00:07.892Z","request_id":"req_011ChLNh4Jt23Y1WqCv35JgZ"}
